 chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2x,-2y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={t}^{2}$ and $y=2t-1$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨2{t}^{2},-2(2t-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{t}^{2},2-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨2{t}^{2},2-4t⟩\\cdot ⟨2t,2⟩ \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}\\cdot 2t+(2-4t)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4{t}^{3}-8t+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(0))] & =4(0)^{3}-8(0)+4 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361440 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361441 13194139535689 true] [17592186361440 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361442 13194139535689 true] [17592186361440 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361443 13194139535689 true] [17592186361440 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361444 13194139535689 true] [17592186361440 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361445 13194139535689 true] [17592186361440 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535689 true] [17592186361440 1041 "selection" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361440 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361443 13194139535689 true] [17592186361440 1110 #uuid "658ce548-a766-5a78-9925-28b8ffd124e1" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361441 1034 "2" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361441 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535689 true] [17592186361441 1111 #uuid "927f2579-8c06-5c1e-8083-4de1953a2c67" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361442 1034 "-3" 13194139535689 true] 