d{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4),\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{2}-3,48,2t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,0,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}}⟩ \\\\  & =({t}^{2}-3)\\cdot 1+48\\cdot 0+2t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}\\cdot \\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}-3+0+2{t}^{2} \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(2))] & =3(2)^{2}-3 \\\\  & =12-3 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361448 13194139535689 true] [17592186361447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361449 13194139535689 true] [17592186361447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361450 13194139535689 true] [17592186361447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361451 13194139535689 true] [17592186361447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361452 13194139535689 true] [17592186361447 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535689 true] [17592186361447 1041 "selection" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361447 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361449 13194139535689 true] [17592186361447 1110 #uuid "51ca6068-4300-5c23-b15f-253600f9d0a4" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361448 1034 "-7" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361448 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535689 true] [17592186361448 1111 #uuid "2d08b5c3-3235-5f80-b1f0-7b298f31a9e2" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361449 1034 "9" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361449 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535689 true] [17592186361449 1111 #uuid "19a87405-8140-5cd0-8a40-e5bb95ff6976" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361450 1034 "10" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361450 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535689 true] [17592186361450 1111 #uuid "a7eff3d1