gned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3),2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2t-2}{5{t}^{2}-2t+10},\\frac{6}{5{t}^{2}-2t+10},\\frac{4t}{5{t}^{2}-2t+10}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{2t-2}{5{t}^{2}-2t+10}\\cdot 1+\\frac{6}{5{t}^{2}-2t+10}\\cdot 0+\\frac{4t}{5{t}^{2}-2t+10}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2t-2+8t}{5{t}^{2}-2t+10} \\\\  & =\\frac{10t-2}{5{t}^{2}-2t+10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(0))] & =\\frac{10(0)-2}{5(0)^{2}-2(0)+10} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361455 13194139535689 true] [17592186361454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361456 13194139535689 true] [17592186361454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361457 13194139535689 true] [17592186361454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361458 13194139535689 true] [17592186361454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361459 13194139535689 true] [17592186361454 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535689 true] [17592186361454 1041 "selection" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361454 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361459 13194139535689 true] [17592186361454 1110 #uuid "9d05aaa6-a0c7-5a98-8fd2-d4bdc2ee5ecb" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361455 1034 "\\frac{3}{10}" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361455 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535689 true] [17592186361455 1111 #uuid "01a30646-a89f-587a-b37d-58b13ba4d78a" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361456 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361456 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535689 true] [17592186361456 1111 #uuid "50ee5d73-2ff7-5c6f-9133-6a1cd5834f01" 13194139535689 true] [17592186361457 1034 "\\frac{8}{13}" 13194139535689 tru